config DRM_ACCEL_EDGETPU
	tristate "Google Edge TPU (gs201) accelerator (Rust)"
	depends on DRM_ACCEL
	depends on RUST
	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on GSA
	select RUST_DRM_GEM_SHMEM_HELPER
	help
	  Rust DRM compute-accelerator driver for the Google Edge TPU built into
	  the Tensor G2 (gs201) SoC, as found in the Pixel Fold (felix). Reuses the
	  hardware knowledge of Google's out-of-tree edgetpu/rio stack but exposes a
	  clean mainline /dev/accel/accelN interface; the DarwiNN/VII runtime lives
	  in userspace.

	  The secure firmware is authenticated and started by GSA over Trusty; the
	  companion edgetpu_gsa module provides that glue, hence the GSA dependency.

	  If M is selected, the modules are edgetpu and edgetpu_gsa.
